Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

YUYUTSAVA depends on third-party packages that are not distributed as part of
this source tree; each is installed separately by the package manager and
remains under its own license. The agent framework and its ecosystem
(deepagents, LangChain, LangGraph, FastAPI, and the LangChain provider
integrations) are MIT-licensed.

Two runtime dependencies are LGPL-licensed:

    pynput    LGPL-3.0    (yuyutsava/events/sources/hotkey.py)
    psycopg   LGPL-3.0    (yuyutsava/storage/, Postgres driver)

Both are imported at runtime as ordinary, independently-installed Python
libraries. Under that arrangement the LGPL imposes no obligation on this
project's own Apache-2.0-licensed source, and none is claimed here.

This changes if YUYUTSAVA is ever redistributed as a *frozen, self-contained
binary* that embeds these libraries — for example a PyInstaller bundle inside
an electron-builder artifact. In that case LGPL-3.0 sections 4 and 5 attach to
the combined work, and the distributor must provide the means to relink
against a modified version of the LGPL component. Anyone packaging YUYUTSAVA
for distribution should confirm this before shipping.

The bundled optional DeepFace integration (yuyutsava/mcp_servers/deepface/)
imports the `deepface` package (MIT) only when the `deepface` extra is
installed; the model weights it downloads at first use carry their own upstream
licenses and are not redistributed here.
